    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** MediaCo is a radio broadcaster pivoting toward digital, with digital ads now nearly half of ad sales and cross-platform momentum cited by management. Revenue is growing, but profitability remains elusive: rising operating costs and a loss from the Sigma Audio Networks investment are widening net losses. Trading is thin and the stock sits below its moving averages; a sharp percentage spike in short interest, although from a negligible base, signals some speculative bearishness amid otherwise sparse market conviction.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management points to cross-platform progress but offers no forward guidance, leaving visibility low. There is little detail on capital allocation or expense discipline as costs rise. The lack of analyst coverage and the absence of a clear profitability path keep the market skeptical about the digital pivot’s ability to create lasting value.",
